        "Why does the Torah repeat the Jewish holidays in Parashat Pinchas after already teaching them in Parashat Emor?\n\nAt first glance, it appears to be unnecessary repetition. But Chazal, the classic commentators, and the Kabbalistic tradition reveal that the two Torah portions are teaching two completely different lessons.\n\nIn this short Torah class we explore:\n\n• Why Emor focuses on the holiness of the festivals\n\n• Why Pinchas focuses almost exclusively on the korbanot\n\n• The deeper difference between sacred time and Divine service\n\n• The mystical explanation from the Zohar and Kabbalah\n\n• How the korbanot drew Divine light into the world\n\nThis class is dedicated לעילוי נשמת Hirsh ben Mark Brants (\"Gosha Brants\"), whose first yahrtzeit falls on 23 Tammuz 5786. May this Torah learning bring an aliyah to his soul.\n\nParashat Pinchas\n\nParashat Emor\n\nJewish holidays\n\nMoedim\n\nKorbanot\n\nTemple sacrifices\n\nBeit Hamikdash\n\nTorah class\n\nWeekly Torah portion\n\nParsha Pinchas\n\nParsha Emor\n\nZohar\n\nKabbalah\n\nJewish festivals\n\nBiblical feasts\n\nHebrew Bible\n\nRabbi Eliyahu Bari\n\nTorah insights\n\nMystical Torah\n\nPeshat and Sod\n\n#ParashatPinchas\n\n#ParashatEmor\n\n#Torah\n\n#Kabbalah\n\n#Zohar\n\n#JewishHolidays\n\n#Korbanot\n\n#RabbiEliyahuBari\n\n#WeeklyParsha\n\n#Judaism"
