        "Watch the complete series in order:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLDKe3hTC3IltlQ3tpgxCWWHWkuxWoDjO3\n\nWhat is the deep connection between the Pesach Seder and the Tefillin Shel Rosh, and how does this relationship reveal the true meaning of the Crown of Redemption? In this powerful and eye-opening class, Rav Eliyahu Bari uncovers a profound spiritual link that transforms how we understand both Pesach and the daily mitzvah of Tefillin.\n\nThe Pesach Seder is not just a commemoration of the Exodus from Egypt—it is a living, experiential journey of redemption. Every element of the Seder is designed to awaken awareness, reshape identity, and guide a person through an internal process of liberation. But what happens after the Seder night ends? How is that redemption carried forward into daily life? This is where the connection to Tefillin Shel Rosh becomes essential.\n\nTefillin Shel Rosh, worn on the head, represents clarity of thought, alignment of the mind, and the elevation of consciousness. It is often described as a form of a “crown,” resting above a person’s intellect and symbolizing higher awareness. Rav Eliyahu Bari explains that just as the Pesach Seder initiates the process of redemption, the Tefillin Shel Rosh sustains and completes it on a daily basis.\n\nThe concept of the Crown of Redemption emerges from this connection. The Seder night plants the seeds of freedom, but the true “crown” is achieved when those insights are internalized and consistently expressed in everyday life. The Tefillin Shel Rosh serves as a daily reminder that redemption is not a one-time event, but an ongoing state of consciousness that must be maintained and renewed.\n\nThis class explores how the structure of the Pesach Seder mirrors the structure of spiritual growth. Each step—from telling the story to eating matzah—parallels stages of internal transformation. Rav Eliyahu Bari shows how these stages correspond to the role of Tefillin Shel Rosh, which binds a person’s thoughts to higher purpose and anchors redemption in the mind.\n\nAnother key insight revealed in this lesson is the idea that true freedom is intellectual and spiritual before it is physical. The Exodus was not only about leaving Egypt, but about removing the limitations of perception and belief. Tefillin Shel Rosh represents this transformation of the mind, turning abstract inspiration into structured awareness and disciplined thinking.\n\nBy understanding the connection between the Pesach Seder and Tefillin Shel Rosh, a person gains a practical framework for living redemption every day. The Crown of Redemption is not distant or abstract—it is built through consistency, awareness, and the ability to carry moments of inspiration into daily action.\n\nThis class will give you a deeper appreciation of both Pesach and Tefillin, revealing how these two mitzvot are intimately connected in guiding a person toward spiritual completion. It offers a powerful perspective on how to move from inspiration to integration, and from momentary insight to lasting transformation.\n\n--- IN THIS VIDEO ---\n\nWhy the Pesach Seder begins the process of redemption\nHow Tefillin Shel Rosh represents the “crown” of spiritual awareness\nPractical ways to carry Seder inspiration into daily life\n\nIf this class gave you a new perspective, make sure to like this video, subscribe for more deep Torah insights, and share it with others who want to grow spiritually. Leave a comment below with your thoughts and how you connect the Seder to your daily life.\n\n#Pesach #Tefillin #TorahWisdom #SpiritualGrowth #JewishLearning #Redemption #Passover #Mitzvot #InnerGrowth #Faith"
