      "title": "Quantum Physics in Pirkei Avot 5/8 – Ethics of Our Fathers – Rav Eliyahu Bari",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xGrC5Rv92R8",
      "description": [
        "If every action you take writes itself into the fabric of reality, where exactly is that information stored? What is the ultimate “hard drive” of the universe—and how did it come into existence? \n\nThe Arizal, Rabbi Isaac Luria, taught that before creation there was only Or Ein Sof—the infinite, boundless light of the Creator. There was no space for independence, no room for free will. To allow a world of choice and moral responsibility to exist, a radical process occurred: Tzimtzum, a withdrawal or concealment of infinite light. This act formed a conceptual vacuum known as the Chalal, an “empty space” in which finite reality could emerge. \n\nBut the Chalal was not truly empty. \n\nThe Arizal offers a striking analogy. Imagine a jar filled with thick oil. When you pour the oil out, the jar appears empty—but a subtle residue clings to its walls. That residue still carries the essence and character of what once filled it. In Kabbalah, this indestructible residue is called the Reshimu—the Trace, the Impression. \n\nThe Reshimu is not poetic symbolism. It is described as the foundational informational imprint of creation. Kabbalistic texts explain that the Reshimu consists of Otiyot—Letters. And letters are not abstract decorations. They are discrete units of structured meaning. In computational language, they function like bits and qubits, fundamental informational building blocks. The Reshimu is the encoded DNA of existence. \n\nModern physics has arrived at a remarkably parallel concept. The Holographic Principle suggests that the information describing a three-dimensional region of space can be fully encoded on a two-dimensional boundary. Reality, in other words, may function like a vast projection from an informational surface. \n\nLurianic Kabbalah describes an almost identical architecture. The physical universe unfolds within the Chalal, yet its structural information is embedded in the surrounding layer of the Reshimu. The boundary holds the code. The world is not self-generating; it is data-driven. \n\nThis convergence between Torah and theoretical physics is not superficial metaphor. It points toward a shared structural intuition: information is more fundamental than matter. Just as black hole event horizons encode physical data, the Reshimu encodes spiritual and existential data. The universe is not built from randomness—it is built from structured divine information. \n\nAnd here is where it becomes personal. \n\nEvery time you act in the physical world, you generate energy, intention, and consequence. According to Torah thought, that energy interacts with the deeper informational layer of reality. Your deeds do not float away into nothingness. They interface with the Reshimu and modify its encoded pattern. The Cosmic Hard Drive is not static; it is responsive. \n\nWhen the Sages teach that “All your deeds are written in a book,” they are describing this very mechanism. The Book is not a celestial diary. It is the dynamic informational substrate of creation itself. Writing is not symbolic—it is ontological. Actions become code. \n\nFrom the perspective of quantum theory, interactions are never lost. Information is conserved. From the perspective of Kabbalah, spiritual impact is never erased. The Reshimu ensures continuity. Together, they describe a universe whose architecture preserves every meaningful imprint. \n\nThis transforms our understanding of responsibility. We are not merely inhabitants of a prewritten system. We are participants in its ongoing compilation. Every choice contributes to the shaping of the cosmic record. The Trace left at the dawn of creation becomes the canvas upon which human freedom paints. \n\nIn this lecture, Rav Eliyahu Bari unpacks the depth of Or Ein Sof, Tzimtzum, Chalal, and Reshimu, connecting them with contemporary discussions about digital reality, holographic encoding, and information theory. The result is a breathtaking synthesis: Torah mysticism and modern physics both describe a universe grounded in indestructible informational structure. \n\nIf the Reshimu is the ultimate hard drive of existence, then nothing truly disappears. The question that remains is even more astonishing: if our actions are encoded permanently, what about our identity? What about the Neshama itself? Is the human soul also a form of indestructible divine code? \n\nIn the next part of this series, we will explore the bold and transformative idea that the soul is not fragile biological output—but eternal spiritual software, designed to transcend physical hardware. \n\n--- IN THIS VIDEO --- \n\nHow Tzimtzum and the Chalal create the architecture for free will \n\nWhy the Reshimu functions as the informational DNA of the universe \n\nWhat it means that your actions modify the cosmic code \n\n#Reshimu #LurianicKabbalah #TorahAndScience #Tzimtzum #OrEinSof #HolographicPrinciple #JewishMysticism #QuantumInformation #RavEliyahuBari #CosmicArchitecture"
      ],
