      "description": [
        "Watch the complete series in order:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLDKe3hTC3Ilu1xDuxglADoBPJjUVq74Vx\n\nWhat if modern quantum physics is uncovering the very same truth that the Torah revealed thousands of years ago? What if the “Heavenly Ledger” described by our Sages is not just a moral metaphor—but the literal architecture of reality itself? \n\nIn this groundbreaking lecture, Rav Eliyahu Bari explores the astonishing convergence between Torah wisdom and cutting-edge science. For generations, we have learned the powerful words from Pirkei Avot: “An eye that sees, an ear that hears, and all your deeds are written in a book.” We were taught that the ledger is open and the hand writes. These teachings shaped our understanding of Hashgacha Pratit, Divine Providence, and personal responsibility. But what if these statements are not poetic symbolism? What if they describe the fundamental structure of the universe? \n\nThis class dives deep into one of the most perplexing problems in theoretical physics: the Black Hole Information Paradox. Modern physicists struggle with a central question in quantum mechanics—can information ever truly be destroyed? The emerging scientific consensus is extraordinary: information is never lost. Even when matter disappears into a black hole, the information encoded within it remains preserved on the event horizon. The universe itself appears to function like a perfect, indestructible recording system. \n\nNow consider the Torah perspective. From the Zohar to Lurianic Kabbalah, from the Maharal of Prague to the Baal Shem Tov, Jewish mystical tradition has long described reality as layered with spiritual imprint and permanent trace. The concept of Reshimu teaches that every spiritual action leaves an eternal mark. Every thought, every word, every deed creates a lasting imprint in the cosmic structure. The world is not a temporary stage—it is a dynamic recording field. \n\nIn this lecture, we carefully examine how the quantum principle of information conservation mirrors the Torah’s teaching that nothing is ever erased. We explore how the “Book of Remembrance” described by our Sages aligns conceptually with the idea that the boundary of a black hole stores encoded information. We analyze how the Neshama, the eternal soul, functions within a universe that never deletes data. And we discuss how Techiyat HaMetim—the Resurrection of the Dead—can be understood through the lens of ultimate information recovery. \n\nThis is not a superficial comparison between science and religion. It is a deep, disciplined exploration of how Torah and quantum physics may be describing the same underlying system from different languages. The Black Hole Information Paradox becomes more than a physics puzzle—it becomes a window into Divine Providence. Hashgacha is no longer abstract; it is woven into the quantum fabric of existence. \n\nFor serious students of Torah, this class offers a powerful strengthening of emunah grounded in intellectual rigor. For seekers of science, it presents a framework in which faith and physics are not enemies but partners in truth. The Eternal Torah Record is not mythology—it may be the operating system of creation. \n\nIf quantum mechanics teaches that no information can ever be destroyed, then every human action carries infinite weight. Every struggle, every hidden act of integrity, every quiet moment of growth is permanently encoded into reality. Nothing vanishes. Nothing is forgotten. The ledger is open. \n\n--- IN THIS VIDEO --- \n\nWhy the Heavenly Ledger appears specifically in the language of Pirkei Avot \n\nHow quantum information theory parallels the Torah concept of Reshimu \n\nWhat this means for daily responsibility and spiritual growth \n\nIf this perspective expanded your understanding of Torah and science, make sure to like this video, subscribe to the channel, and share it with someone searching for deeper truth. Leave a comment with your thoughts on the connection between quantum physics and Divine Providence. Your engagement helps spread serious Torah learning to the world. \n\n#QuantumPhysics #TorahAndScience #JewishThought #BlackHoleParadox #HashgachaPratit #KabbalahWisdom #InformationTheory #PirkeiAvot #Reshimu #RavEliyahuBari"
      ],
