        "Смотрите всю серию по порядку:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLDKe3hTC3Ilv6WAezCB-Sy4ur_7mH52ck\n\nWhat was so special about the Cave of Machpela that Avraham insisted on purchasing it in full, and in private? In this class, Rav Eliyahu Bari explores the deep mystical meaning behind Maaras HaMachpela as revealed by Ramad Vali.\n\nAfter the death of Sarah, Avraham turns to the people of Cheis and calls himself both “a stranger and a resident.” Ramad Vali explains that he was truly a stranger — but now, with Sarah buried there, part of him had become a permanent resident. The soul is connected to where the body is buried, and Avraham knew he would one day be buried there as well.\n\nAvraham urgently sought to bury Sarah without delay, to prevent impure spiritual forces from attaching to her holy body. While the people of Cheis wanted her buried among them, Avraham refused — he did not want Sarah to be exposed to the spiritual contamination of the wicked. He insisted on a separate place, protected and pure.\n\nThat place was Maaras HaMachpela — the \"double cave.\" On a surface level, it’s called “doubled” because of its two tiers. But Ramad Vali explains its mystical meaning: the cave represents the gateway to Gan Eden, and it mirrors the two letters hei (ה) in the Divine Name. These represent two spiritual gates — the upper and lower “hei” — which righteous souls pass through upon leaving this world.\n\nAvraham intentionally concealed the cave's spiritual power by referring to it merely as “the edge of the field.” Had the people of Cheis understood its holiness, they would have denied him access. Ephron, unaware of its depth, saw no divine light and readily agreed to sell.\n\nThe pasuk in Yeshayahu (26:2) says: “Open the gates, and let the righteous nation enter” — in plural — hinting to these two gates of holiness that Avraham saw.\n\nThe name \"Machpela\" can also be read as “Hei–Machpela” — the doubled ‘hei’ — referencing the Divine Name, and hinting at the cave's function as a portal between worlds.\n\n--- IN THIS VIDEO ---\n\nWhy does Avraham call himself both a stranger and a resident?\n\nWhat spiritual danger was Avraham trying to avoid by burying Sarah quickly?\n\nWhy was the Cave of Machpela called “doubled”?\n\nWhat are the two gates of holiness, and how are they connected to the Divine Name?\n\nHow did Avraham see spiritual light in the cave that no one else could see?\n\nThis class will open your eyes to the deep spiritual architecture of the Torah’s most famous burial site, and how Avraham’s foresight secured more than just land — he secured a doorway to eternity.\n\n👍 Like the video, ✅ Subscribe to the channel, and 💬 leave a comment:\nHave you ever thought about what happens to the soul after death? Share your thoughts.\n\n#RamadVali #ChayeiSarah #CaveOfMachpela #AvrahamAndSarah #RavEliyahuBari #GanEden #DoubleCave #JewishMysticism #BurialInTorah #KabbalahClass #TorahInsights #SpiritualGates #HolyLand"
